{
  "draft_response": "Thanks for the suggestion—scheduling exports directly to your S3 bucket sounds like it would definitely save time for your data team.\n\nTo help us route this to the right product owners and capture the requirements accurately, could you share a few details?\n1) Which export(s) are you looking to schedule (which dataset/table/reports in our product)?\n2) Preferred file format(s) (CSV only, or other formats as well)?\n3) Schedule configuration: what day/time and timezone should run, and do you need a simple weekly cadence or more control?\n4) S3 specifics: bucket name plus whether you have a desired object key/prefix (e.g., folder path), and your region.\n5) Auth/permissions approach: should the connection use your credentials (customer-managed) or another method you already use with us (if applicable)?\n6) Overwrite/versioning and naming: should each run overwrite a fixed object name, or create uniquely named files per run?\n7) Do you need any notifications or logging when exports succeed/fail?\n\nOnce we have these, we can confirm what’s feasible and log this as a formal feature request for evaluation. Since you mentioned this isn’t blocking, we’ll align on next steps after review.",
  "tone": "clarifying",
  "promised_actions": [
    "Route the request to product owners for evaluation as a formal feature request",
    "Use the details provided to confirm feasibility and align on next steps"
  ],
  "safety_notes": [
    "Do not claim availability or delivery of the feature; only promise routing and review.",
    "Avoid committing to timeline, SLA, or specific implementation details until requirements are reviewed by the product team."
  ]
}
